{"kind":"event","event_id":2306,"event_uid":"01M2HWJBZRX8GVGRGRBTVGWWMQ","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":127,"issue_uid":"01M2HWDE5ZEECTZEM207HKFXK2","issue_short_id":"fxk2","actor":"impl:1@run-7","hlc_physical_ms":1789454266360,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"be90d4d4b77dae3906f1277bcf34582c3bc7b27f1daec9a554c353014819b031","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HWJBZQ6GP791XXH8P797DT","author":"impl:1@run-7","body":"Task 1 approach: put the `window.__TINYAPP_STORE__` assignment in one place — `createTodosStore` in client/src/storeData.ts — set when the factory is handed a seed, and `delete`d when it is not, so leg (b) holds no matter which order the peer exam runs its legs in (bun runs a file's tests in one process, so a stale handle from leg (a) would otherwise survive into leg (b)). Typed through a `declare global` Window merge in storeData.ts (vite-env.d.ts stays the home of __TINYAPP_SEED__). Store.tsx already passes the seed it read at mount, so the seeded render gets the handle for free and no second code path is needed. AGENTS.md gets the exact Key Files sentence the task dictates — seeded page sets the handle, normal page does not, and the seeded page is the one that starts neither link.","created_at":"2026-09-15T06:37:46.359212316Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T06:37:46.36Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2307,"event_uid":"01M2HWKNKQRVWWA2VN5H0FCBA0","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":127,"issue_uid":"01M2HWDE5ZEECTZEM207HKFXK2","issue_short_id":"fxk2","actor":"exam:1@run-7","hlc_physical_ms":1789454308983,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"d58b9a7a128224ef6669cd9fedd013ae9ed4ef3cdd7abdaee4f2f931d4b8224e","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HWKNKPGEZ54Q79682PJHR2","author":"exam:1@run-7","body":"examiner, approach for the exam at `client/test/seeded-store-global.test.ts`:\n\nReading of the legs I am encoding, so a later session does not have to re-derive them:\n\n- **Leg (a) [M1] is exercised through a *render of `Store`*, not through a bare `createTodosStore(seed)` call.** The task leaves the implementer a choice of two places for the assignment (inside `createTodosStore` when handed a seed, or in `Store`'s seeded branch). Only the render exercises both: a direct `createTodosStore(seed)` call would be silently red against the `Store.tsx` placement, which the task explicitly permits. Leg (a)'s own words — \"the store created as the page creates it\" — say the same thing. The exam therefore renders `Store` under a `Provider`, reads the app's store back with a `useStore(STORE_ID)` probe (the BASE `seeded-store.test.ts` pattern), and compares `window.__TINYAPP_STORE__.getContent()` against it. Deep-equality, not identity: M1 asks for the same `[tables, values]` pair, not the same object.\n- The seed is **read from `state-exams/seeds/two-open-todos.json` on disk**, resolved through `import.meta.dir`, and `<first id>` is the first key of its `todos` table. The expected post-mutation content is derived from that same file rather than hardcoded, so the exam stays exact without pinning a file it does not own.\n- **Leg (b) [M2] deletes `__TINYAPP_STORE__` before the unseeded render.** Leg (a) runs first in the same process and sets it; without the delete the negative control would be asserting against leg (a)'s leftover rather than against this render.\n- **Leg (c) [M3], \"WebSocket stubbed\":** counted on *both* readings — the global `WebSocket` constructor is replaced with a recording class *and* `reconnecting-websocket` is module-mocked with one, both incrementing a single counter. `Store.tsx` reaches a socket through `ReconnectingWebSocket`, so a stub on the global alone would record zero for a reason that has nothing to do with the seeded branch. The persister and synchronizer factories are mocked too (as BASE does) — not a leg, just what keeps the unseeded render inert and off the network.\n- **Leg (d) [M4]** is replicated in the exam as the second `Run:` line's own check: the `## Key Files`…`## Working Method` slice of `AGENTS.md`, newlines flattened, matched against `/__TINYAPP_STORE__.*normal page/`. Nothing stronger — the run-6 inversion the Context warns about (writing that a *normal* page starts neither link) is a wording trap the Proof does not machine-check, and inventing a negative regex for it would be the exam over-reaching past its own contract. An implementer reading this: the tree is that the *seeded* page starts neither.\n\nExpected at BASE: legs (a) and (d) red (no global, no sentence), legs (b) and (c) green — (b) and (c) are the negative control and the kept BASE rule, and are green by construction.","created_at":"2026-09-15T06:38:28.982459495Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T06:38:28.983Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":2308,"event_uid":"01M2HWMJ8RFVE3WYH885WSS8AC","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":33,"project_uid":"01M2HSJCAB4WXJ7C6XEG23B869","project_name":"popmechanic-tinyapp-fixture","issue_id":127,"issue_uid":"01M2HWDE5ZEECTZEM207HKFXK2","issue_short_id":"fxk2","actor":"impl:1@run-7","hlc_physical_ms":1789454338328,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"51e116b3049be4589f46499cad40cacf61c0a6f21a7b43c2d29b4a4de92200bd","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2HWMJ8PS1XV59JE21YHM5F2","author":"impl:1@run-7","body":"Landed. One decision a later session would otherwise rediscover: `createTodosStore` does not merely *set* the handle when seeded, it `delete`s `window.__TINYAPP_STORE__` when it is called without a seed. That is what makes M2/leg (b) order-independent — bun runs a file's tests in one process, so without the delete a handle set by leg (a) would still be on `window` when leg (b) asks for `undefined`. The seeded-store.test.ts leg (g) assertion pins that clearing behaviour on the render path too. Nothing was added to Store.tsx beyond a comment: the seed it already reads at mount and passes to the factory is the only trigger, so there is exactly one place the handle is written. Proofs green: seeded-store.test.ts 2/2, AGENTS.md Key Files grep, bun run typecheck; full suite 119/119.","created_at":"2026-09-15T06:38:58.326767251Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T06:38:58.328Z"}
